description:
Design a 16-bit binary adder that computes the sum of two 16-bit inputs (A and B). The output S represents the lower 16 bits of the sum, while the output C indicates the carry-out generated during the addition process. This module effectively combines the input bits, accounting for any overflow that may occur when adding the two 16-bit numbers.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] A, B,
    output [15:0] S,
    output C
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] A, B,
    output [15:0] S,
    output C
    );wire [15:0] temp;
    wire [16:0] sum;

    assign temp = A ^ B;
    assign sum = {1'b0, A} + {1'b0, B};
    assign S = sum[15:0];
    assign C = sum[16];

endmodule

