description:
Design a 64-bit shift register-based counter with a 4-bit output. On each rising edge of the clock, if the reset (active low) is not asserted, the most significant bit (bit 63) is toggled, while all other bits are shifted right by one position. The least significant 4 bits of the register are then output as the counter value Q. This module essentially captures the state of a shifting pattern, allowing for the observation of the lower 4 bits as a controlled counter.
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [3:0]    Q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [3:0]    Q
);reg [63:0] pipeline_reg;

always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin
  if (~rst_n) begin
    pipeline_reg <= 64'b0;
    Q <= 4'b0;
  end else begin
    pipeline_reg[63] <= ~pipeline_reg[62];
    pipeline_reg[62:0] <= pipeline_reg[63:1];
    Q <= pipeline_reg[3:0];
  end
end

endmodule

