description:
Design a glitch filter that stabilizes the output against rapid changes in the input. The module uses a delayed signal to determine when the input has been stable for at least one clock cycle, and it outputs the stable state of the input after confirming it hasn't fluctuated. This design effectively reduces the impact of transient noise or glitches on the output signal.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);reg delayed_in;
  reg prev_out;

  assign out = prev_out;

  always @(in) begin
    if (in == delayed_in) begin
      prev_out = in;
      delayed_in <= in;
    end else begin
      delayed_in <= delayed_in;
    end
  end

endmodule

