description:
Design a clock division circuit that converts a 50 MHz input clock signal into a 1 kHz output clock signal. The module includes a reset input to initialize the counter and control the output clock. A counter increments on the rising edge of the input clock and toggles the output clock signal after counting to 25,000, effectively dividing the frequency by 50,000. This design purpose is to facilitate lower frequency clock signals for timing applications or to drive circuits that require slower clock rates.
module top_module(
	input clk_50M,
	input rst,
	output clk_1Khz
);

