description:
Design a Power-On Reset (POR) circuit that generates a reset signal for a fixed duration upon the assertion of a power-on (por) signal. The module employs a counter that counts down from a maximum value when por goes high, asserting the reset (rst) signal during this countdown. The reset signal is synchronized with the clock (clk) to ensure proper timing. Additionally, the reset signal remains high as long as either the power-on signal or the reset condition is active, effectively ensuring that the system initializes correctly upon power-up.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input por,
